# Data files (optional - uncomment if you don't want to commit data)
# data/*.csv
# data/*.json

# docs/data is a build artifact: the deploy workflow copies data/ -> docs/data/
# fresh on every run for the GitHub Pages upload. It should NOT be committed —
# doing so just duplicates the entire data/ directory in every commit's tree
# and, since nothing ever re-commits it, it silently goes stale vs. the real
# data/ history anyway. Run `git rm -r --cached docs/data` once to untrack the
# existing copy (see project docs for the full command).
docs/data/

